**`app/javascript/readingTime/formatReadingTime.js`**
```js
export function formatReadingTime(minutes) {
  // Negated comparison so non-numeric input (NaN) also falls back to "1 min read"
  if (!(minutes > 1)) {
    return '1 min read';
  }

  return `${Math.ceil(minutes)} min read`;
}
```

- **Up to one minute:** 0, negative numbers, 0.2 and 1 all return "1 min read".
- **Above one minute:** the number is rounded up, so 1.01 gives "2 min read" and 4.5 gives "5 min read".
- **Bad input:** I wrote the check as `!(minutes > 1)` so `undefined` and `NaN` also return "1 min read" instead of "NaN min read".

**`app/javascript/readingTime/__tests__/formatReadingTime.test.js`** follows the same layout as the existing tests in `utilities/__tests__`. It covers the one-minute-and-under cases, bad input, rounding up, and whole minutes.

